# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# Every value below is a SENTENCE SAYING WHERE TO GET IT rather than a
# placeholder, so a new contributor does not have to guess which dashboard page
# to open. Follow that convention when adding a variable.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed `VITE_` to client code. Everything in
# this file ships inside the JS bundle and is readable from devtools, so NOTHING
# SECRET MAY BE ADDED HERE. The publishable key is safe by design - RLS and the
# grants in supabase/migrations are what protect the data, not the key.
#
# NOTE: Vite resolves env files relative to its own root, which is the package
# it is building (`games/math-blaster/`), so it needs `envDir` pointed back at
# the repo root for this file's location to work. That is `envDir: '../..'` -
# a depth counted from the package, which the workspace move already changed
# once. Get it wrong and every `VITE_*` reads `undefined` and the game falls
# back to local-only, which looks exactly like working software.

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL="Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > Data API > Project URL. For the staging project svelte-games-met-st this is https://wyfceserpwwkxowauyld.supabase.co"

# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys > publishable (formerly 'anon'). This is the ONLY Supabase value that may be committed - see ROADMAP.md invariant 12 - but keep it here rather than hardcoded so a project swap is one file."

# VITE_VT_IDENTITY_BASE="Where the Varsity Tutors student experience is mounted, as a same-origin PATH - '/learner'. NEVER an origin: its session cookies are httpOnly and SameSite=Lax, so a cross-origin request carries none of them and no CORS header rescues that. Absent (the default) means a standalone build that makes no requests and runs exactly as it did before identity existed. Locally, point a dev-server proxy at the student experience and set this to the path you proxied."
